**wordWrap(text, width)**

Write `wordWrap(text, width)`: split `text` into lines of at most `width` characters, breaking only at spaces. A word longer than `width` gets a line of its own. Return the lines as an array (`[]` for empty text).

```js
function wordWrap(text, width) {
  // TODO
  return [text];
